- What optimizations reduce time to O(n^2) or enable pruning of the i-loop?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests dynamic programming with multiple constraints: non-adjacent blocks, exact block count, and reconstruction requirements.

## Key Concepts
- Disjoint blocks with at least one-element gap between consecutive blocks
- dp[i][t] transitions for skipping elements vs. ending a block
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sum queries
- Backpointers for reconstructing the chosen subarray endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const prefix = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) prefix[i] = prefix[i - 1] + A[i - 1];

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      // Skip element i
      if (dp[i - 1][t] >= dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
        prev[i][t] = { skipped: true };
      }
      // End a block at i
      for (let s = 1; s <= i; s++) {
        const prevIdx = s >= 2 ? s - 2 : 0;
        const val = dp[prevIdx][t - 1] + (prefix[i] - prefix[s - 1]) - c;
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          prev[i][t] = { skipped: false, start: s };
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruction
  const result = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (i > 0 && t > 0) {
    const state = prev[i][t];
    if (state.skipped) {
      i--;
    } else {
      result.push({ start: state.start, end: i });
      i = state.start - 2;
      t--;
    }
  }
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks: result.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine subarray maxima with partition DP, requiring both maximization and reconstruction of multiple intervals. It exercises careful indexing and boundary handling.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays with a cap k
- Precomputation of maxSub for O(1) subarray maxima
- 2D DP with reconstruction pointers
- Time/space tradeoffs and edge cases (k=0, equal values)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueWithKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const maxSub = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let m = -Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      m = Math.max(m, A[r]);
      maxSub[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      let best = dp[i-1][t];
      let bestJ = -1;
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = maxSub[j-1][i-1] + dp[j-1][t-1];
        if (val > best) { best = val; bestJ = j; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = best; take[i][t] = bestJ;
    }
  }
  const res = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const j = take[i][t];
    if (j === -1) break;
    res.push([j-1, i-1]);
    i = j - 1;
    t--;
  }
  res.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], subarrays: res};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests comprehensive DP design for partitioning problems with nonlinear segment costs involving both min and sum operations, requiring careful handling of base cases and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-dimensional DP over partition indices
- Range minimum query optimization within transitions
- Complete solution from base cases through reconstruction
- Space-time tradeoffs and optimization strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Initialize DP table and parent pointers
dp[0][0] = 0;
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
  dp[i][1] = rangeMin(1, i) * prefix[i];
  parent[i][1] = 0;
}

// Fill DP table
for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
  for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let p = t-1; p < i; p++) {
      const segVal = rangeMin(p+1, i) * (prefix[i] - prefix[p]);
      const total = dp[p][t-1] + segVal;
      if (total > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = total;
        parent[i][t] = p;
      }
    }
  }
}

// Reconstruct segments
let i = n, t = k;
while (t > 0) {
  const p = parent[i][t];
  segments[t] = [p+1, i];
  i = p;
  t--;
}
```

